<title>USA: Netherlands top source for NY June cut-flower imports.</title>
<headline>Netherlands top source for NY June cut-flower imports.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands was the main source of flown cut-flower imports to New York in June with 27,205 cartons, sharply down on the previous year's 51,901, USDA monthly import figures show.</p>
<p>No immediate explanation for the decline was available.</p>
<p>Top 10 Suppliers of Flown Cut Flower Import to NYK ( in cartons)</p>
<p>			    June 1997     June 1996</p>
<p> The Netherlands	 27,205	     51,901</p>
<p> Israel		     8,449		7,109</p>
<p> Ecuador		    5,887		5,835</p>
<p> Colombia		   2,642		7,729</p>
<p> Thailand		   1,402		2,416</p>
<p> Dominican Republic     1,378		1,663</p>
<p> Italy			1,366		1,935</p>
<p> Zimbabwe		   1,040		1,890</p>
<p> Mexico			 790		1,620</p>
<p> Morocco			492		  702</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
